1
00:00:06,580 --> 00:00:10,120
You know so much about the wildlife here, PK.

2
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:11,520
How come?

3
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:18,773
My family are San, bush people, and I learned about nature from the time when I was a child.

4
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:21,258
I was born in the Kalahari.

5
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:24,940
And you grew up and found your wife here?

6
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:29,340
Yes, finding a wife here was very interesting.

7
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:31,500
Tell us more.

8
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:36,072
Yes, let’s say a young man wants to marry a girl.

9
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:43,874
So he has to ask her father and he says before you can marry my daughter, you have to do a task.

10
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:44,880
OK.

11
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:49,740
So what type of task does the young man have to do, PK?

12
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:57,060
Well, for example, he has to show that he can take a kill away from a lion.

13
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:02,700
What do you mean ‘take a kill away from a lion’?

14
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:08,480
Well, imagine a lion kills an antelope or another large animal.

15
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:15,460
The young man has to find that lion and get the meat, so he can show that he has courage.

16
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:18,797
That’s important for his future family.

17
00:01:18,797 --> 00:01:22,360
Wow, but how can you do that?

18
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:26,420
How can you find a lion and its kill?

19
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:28,073
You have to look.

20
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:31,900
You have to look for the big birds, the vultures.

21
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:36,096
They are watching the lion because they want some of the meat.

22
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:41,200
OK, so let’s say you find the lion and its kill.

23
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:44,120
How can you then get the meat?

24
00:01:44,860 --> 00:01:45,860
Isn’t that dangerous?

25
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:49,320
Yes, of course the lion is dangerous.

26
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:52,960
You mustn’t take the meat away from the lion at night.

27
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:55,798
You have to do that during the day.

28
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:57,220
Why’s that?

29
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:59,966
During the day it’s very hot.

30
00:01:59,966 --> 00:02:03,820
And the big cats can’t run fast when it’s hot.

31
00:02:04,580 --> 00:02:09,020
A man can run even when it’s very hot, but lions can’t.

32
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:09,680
No?

33
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:11,740
No, they can’t.

34
00:02:11,740 --> 00:02:18,280
When they eat some meat, they feel very, very hot and get very tired.

35
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:24,700
So they often just lie around and they sleep all the time during the day.

36
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:29,467
At night they are more dangerous because they don’t sleep.

37
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:33,600
And at night their eyes are better than your eyes.

38
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:36,900
So you can’t get the kill from the lion at night.

39
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:41,360
OK, so you have to do that during the day.

40
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:46,540
But what do you do to get the kill from the lion?

41
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:47,760
OK.

42
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:51,862
So let’s say the lion is sleeping.

43
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:55,578
You hold your spear in your hand.

44
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:58,960
You have to be very quiet.

45
00:02:58,960 --> 00:03:02,240
And you go up to that lion.

46
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:06,440
Do you attack him with your spear?

47
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:07,980
Kill him?

48
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:10,780
No, no, no, no.

49
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:16,280
You just go up to him and shout, ‘Arrrrggggghhhhh!’

50
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:25,775
You mustn’t hurt him or kill him, just surprise him, shock him, so he runs away.

51
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:27,180
Wow!
